{
  "configuration_id": "config_038",
  "reason": "The best result so far is config_039 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted fusion, acc=0.7250), which shows a substantial ~7-point gain over the best RNA-only multi-profile model (0.6530). However, we have no direct comparison of fusion strategy in the multimodal setting. Config_038 is identical to config_039 except it uses concat instead of weighted fusion, isolating exactly one variable. This tells us whether the multimodal gain requires learned cross-modal weighting or whether a simple concatenation suffices. Understanding this is critical: if concat performs comparably, the design space simplifies considerably; if weighted fusion is clearly superior, it indicates the two modalities contribute non-uniformly and the interaction is informative. Under a limited budget, this single-variable A/B test against the current best configuration is the highest-information-per-experiment choice, directly informing whether to invest further in fusion complexity or shift attention to other design axes (e.g., image encoder choice)."
}

